  {
   "id": 646494,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>A singer sold two types of tickets to a performance, seated tickets and standing-room tickets.</p>\n<span>   <ul><li><span><span>Seated tickets cost $25.</span></span></li>\n  <li><span>Standing-room tickets cost $15.</span></li>\n  <li><span>More than 60 tickets were sold.</span></li>\n  <li><span>More than $1,200 was made from selling tickets.</span><p></p>\n</li></ul></span>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Which of the following ticket combinations is possible given the situation described here?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1272761,
     "content_html": "20 seated tickets and 50 standing-room tickets"
    },
    {
     "id": 1272762,
     "content_html": "10 seated tickets and 60 standing-room tickets"
    },
    {
     "id": 1272763,
     "content_html": "40 seated tickets and 19 standing-room tickets"
    },
    {
     "id": 1272764,
     "content_html": "14 seated tickets and 55 standing-room tickets"
    }
   ],
